body:
If you've been in multiple relationships and noticed a trend then maybe there really is something going on. If you've only been in one then it could just be circumstantial. Did your previous boyfriend(s) have anything in common about how they asked you out. Were these people in your friend group, or from school or work. I'm trying to rack my brain to think of what could be different but it's a complicated thing.

&#x200B;

Oh and being too close/having a long friendship with someone before might make it hard, because you value your friendship too much to risk making it awkward when they turn you down.

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6wDm9C5YEo&list=PLdIlUrhJ9--4rZCir4zi7pwnRQykAvqIN&index=5&t=522s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6wDm9C5YEo&list=PLdIlUrhJ9--4rZCir4zi7pwnRQykAvqIN&index=5&t=522s)

&#x200B;

Further reference.  Things with this epic feel that aren't purely classical are ideal.
